    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-upside profile of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (70.30), whose elite speed and prime spot at the top of the order make him our strongest play despite a challenging matchup against Abbott. While **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) and **Yordan Alvarez** (61.80) also project as primary engines, **Kazuma Okamoto** (61.78) is the most compelling value play; his matchup against M\u00e1rquez is the most favorable on the board, allowing his power to shine against an SP_xERA of 5.58. We are navigating significant headwinds, most notably the daunting task of facing Skubal with both **Trea Turner** (55.76) and **Kyle Schwarber** (54.35). While their raw talent keeps them in the start range, their efficiency scores are hampered by the elite SP skill and negative platoon leverage, necessitating a focus on our speed-heavy bench should early-game defensive substitutions occur.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Carson Benge** (40.59), who sat right on the precipice of our 40.0 efficiency threshold. He was ultimately bypassed due to a unfavorable L/L platoon matchup that suppressed his base projection, failing to provide enough projected value to displace lower-scoring but higher-ceiling starters like **Christian Yelich** (53.19). Meanwhile, we have intentionally benched **Gary Sanchez** (37.37), **Dillon Dingler** (35.33), and **Lars Nootbaar** (35.14) to preserve our season-long game caps; their sub-40 scores indicate that the risk of limited production against elite arms like Skenes and Wheeler outweighs their potential to help us climb the league standings today. Owners should monitor the wind and late-breaking weather reports, as the conditions affecting **Lars Nootbaar** remain a secondary factor for potential mid-game adjustments if the wind profile shifts significantly.",
